"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Live-run finding + design pivot (2026-08-14).\n\nRan the first live-Cloud draft against REB+DIG on an isolated S3 store copy. The first scenario FAILED at the read-only preview step (no production impact): the harness seeded dummy project keys (REBEMPTY, REBGHOST) that exist only in the mapping, never in Jira. Real Jira parse-errors on a non-existent key ('the value \"rebempty\" does not exist for the field \"project\"'), acli exits 1, and the inbound fetcher (_build_snapshot, no per-project try/except) propagates that and aborts the whole pass. The stateful fake transport all other stories use returned empty for unknown projects, masking this. Reproduced read-only: 'project = REBEMPTY' errors; 'project = REB' with an impossible filter returns []. Engine review found NO contract that a mapped-but-absent project should be tolerated — the inbound search is deliberately fail-closed (correct for a bridge).\n\nRoot cause: harness design flaw (not a product bug) — the plan assumed querying a non-existent project returns empty; it errors. Compounded by only two real Cloud projects existing, which cannot faithfully model three repo shapes + empty + unknown paths.\n\nPivot (user-directed, option A + DC): rework the rehearsal to run against the ephemeral Jira DC instance the existing tests/external/live_jira_dc harness stands up in CI, where we hold admin rights and can create/destroy throwaway projects per run. This makes the rehearsal a reproducible, CI-verified green run in the jira-dc-harness job (not a manual operator-attested Cloud run), dissolves the two-project constraint, models 'empty' with a real empty project, and models 'unknown' as its true fail-closed behaviour. Description + file_impact + ACs rewritten accordingly; the ACs now require a green DC run. Re-running plan-review next.","timestamp":1786743675021643001}],"created_at":1786164881990750001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"e4cc1ad7-3ac2-417a-aae8-61fa428133d9","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"c927-0a68-4465-42a2"},{"link_uuid":"d4a33e4a-0556-477a-ba73-a592ee3e08a2","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"cef7-7ac5-18e6-41a3"},{"link_uuid":"15e35460-3f6b-4a25-bd49-fa9df967154d","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"1734-7c6d-5a6a-48fd"},{"link_uuid":"0b53795d-6ba9-49b9-af39-47c9b590199a","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"d19d-7f60-0137-475a"},{"link_uuid":"8a0abae0-167f-48c3-8e98-85df37e59e05","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"462d-8d84-122a-4812"},{"link_uuid":"bc0f8e53-717a-498a-9555-980bbbfb552a","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"67f9-4a07-9667-446a"},{"link_uuid":"2be65bbd-6672-4717-8fea-3c42072144d9","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"7032-d9f3-ed89-4f7b"},{"link_uuid":"669a9b79-bc2b-42dd-bb84-bd45f1194f8d","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"273a-ae7d-23ac-40c2"},{"link_uuid":"e9c3996e-4ecb-4488-a1aa-6281c3490c99","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"4631-5598-7127-4a56"},{"link_uuid":"dfdecdcd-eff3-4a4b-83a2-04bed4207ddf","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"ce02-47ed-6505-4925"},{"link_uuid":"7059b72f-5f3b-4f7e-b46b-40c95fa5738c","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"a33c-9001-9d86-4e59"},{"link_uuid":"f3a9f86e-48fa-461a-b3a1-40b6d1214eb4","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9c22-f26d-47e9-4288"},{"link_uuid":"1bc8e630-2f18-4bb4-ac03-9fb9eb388c35","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8c08-305f-3faf-489d"},{"link_uuid":"cac19e6b-3355-4117-b814-44c0bbc344a8","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e917-ab1e-a5c3-4994"},{"link_uuid":"da74379b-c12a-4b01-bd3d-e8d775ce65aa","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b4f6-6c5f-1671-4554"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nEvery other story in this epic is validated against fixtures and a stateful fake transport — the\nright tier for each. But a fake cannot reach the failure modes that only appear against a real\ntracker: real JQL over several projects, real per-project key allocation and issue creation, and the\none that matters most — whether a pass scoped to one project can contaminate another. It is the\njustified live canary the shared test-design standard allows for external-service mapping.\n\nA first live-Cloud draft (against the shared REB + DIG projects) surfaced two flaws the fake had\nmasked, making live Cloud the wrong tier:\n\n1. Non-existent project keys parse-ERROR, they do not return empty. The draft modelled the\n   \"configured but empty\" and \"unknown to the tracker\" paths with keys that live only in the mapping,\n   never in Jira. Real Jira rejects `project = REBEMPTY` (`the value 'rebempty' does not exist for the\n   field 'project'`), acli exits non-zero, and because the inbound fetcher fans a per-project query\n   out with no per-project try/except (`fetcher.py` `_build_snapshot`), that aborts the ENTIRE pass.\n   The fake returned empty, so nothing caught it. No contract says a mapped-but-absent project is\n   tolerated; the inbound search is deliberately fail-closed, the safe posture for a bridge.\n2. Only two real Cloud projects exist. Modelling three repo shapes (one/two/zero repos), an empty\n   project, and an unknown-project fail-closed path needs more isolated projects than two shared\n   production projects supply, and throwaway Cloud projects are not available here.\n\n## Approach\n\nRehearse against the ephemeral Jira Data Center instance the existing DC harness\n(`tests/external/live_jira_dc/`) already stands up in CI, where we hold admin rights and create and\ndestroy throwaway projects per run. This dissolves both flaws and makes the rehearsal a reproducible,\nCI-verified green run on every build (the `jira-dc-harness` job) rather than a manual attested\nlive-Cloud step. The isolated store copy is the harness's existing local/file-based copy\n(`REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=off`); no S3 remote is involved.\n\nA per-run fixture provisions four scratch projects via the harness's bug-3fe5-hardened provisioning\n(pinned `_PROJECT_TEMPLATE`; `_assert_project_capabilities` verifies issue types/fields first, no\nsilent degrade), each a random `RBJ`-prefixed key, and tears them all down on\nevery exit path: P_ONE -> one repo, P_TWO -> two repos, P_ZERO -> zero repos, P_LEGACY -> the legacy\ndefault. \"Configured but empty of issues\" is now a REAL project that simply returns `[]` in a pass,\nnever a non-existent key. \"Unknown to Jira\" is modelled as its true product behaviour: a key never\ncreated is configured and the harness asserts the pass FAILS CLOSED (the per-project search raises,\nthe pass writes nothing).\n\nDry-run gating is the contamination control: each mutating scenario runs `bridge preview` first and\nasserts the previewed mutation set contains ONLY targets in the intended project (empty intersection\nagainst every other configured project) before `bridge sync` runs — every mutating pass, including\nany binding setup sync, is preview-gated first. The per-mutation target project each intersection is\ncomputed against is read from the preview plan: the Jira key prefix for an outbound UPDATE, and the\n`_bridge_target_project` field for an outbound CREATE (which has no key yet).\n\nCleanup runs on every exit path: session-scoped finalizers DELETE each scratch project\n(`/rest/api/2/project/{key}`, poll-until-404), which removes its issues; per-run random keys mean no\nrun touches another's data, and a session guard refuses to start if a prior `RBJ*` project leaked.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `tests/external/live_jira_dc/conftest.py` (edit) — add a session-scoped `scratch_projects` fixture\n  that yields N verified scratch projects, REUSING the existing in-conftest provisioning\n  (`_create_scratch_project` / `_assert_project_capabilities` / `_random_project_key` / `_request`),\n  and tears them all down. Nothing is relocated: ccf6 and\n  `test_live_jira_dc_conftest.py::test_the_monkeypatched_surface_is_still_defined_in_conftest` require\n  `_request` and the provisioning helpers to stay DEFINED in conftest (two unit tests monkeypatch\n  `_request` in conftest's namespace, and moving them fails open to live HTTP), so the cluster is\n  reused in place, never moved. The module-size cap applies only to `src/rebar`, so this test file\n  may grow.\n- `tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_multi_project_rehearsal.py` (new) — the scenarios and per-run\n  fixtures (four scratch projects, isolated DC store copy mapped for them, DC-pointed bridge config).\n- `docs/jira-sync-setup.md` (edit) — runbook: the rehearsal now runs against the ephemeral DC\n  instance in CI (and locally via `make jira-dc-up`), replacing the live-Cloud section.\n- `tests/external/live_multi_project/conftest.py` (delete) and\n  `tests/external/live_multi_project/test_multi_project_rehearsal.py` (delete) — the flawed\n  live-Cloud-only draft, replaced by the DC rehearsal.\n\n## Testing\n\nTier: a live end-to-end rehearsal against a real Jira DC instance — permitted by the shared standard\nfor external-service mapping when a fake cannot reach the mechanism (genuine cross-project isolation,\nreal JQL over several projects). Gated to the opt-in external suite (`REBAR_RUN_EXTERNAL=1`, the\nDC-readiness sentinel) and run in the `jira-dc-harness` CI job (`pytest -m external\ntests/external/live_jira_dc`) on a native-amd64 runner; a new file there is collected automatically.\nThe nine scenarios are the Acceptance Criteria below, each preview-gated then applied.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The rehearsal provisions its throwaway scratch projects with the hardened pinned template and\n      verifies their capabilities before any scenario runs; checked by asserting each created project\n      reports the required issue types/fields (a degrade fails provisioning, not a later scenario).\n- [ ] Issues created in two scratch projects are both ingested in one pass with the correct source\n      project and repos recorded; checked by querying both projects and asserting both tickets' fields.\n- [ ] Rebar-created tickets targeting each project land in that project only; checked by querying the\n      projects and asserting each issue exists in exactly one.\n- [ ] A ticket with an explicit empty project creates no issue in any project; checked by a post-run\n      query of every scratch project finding no issue for it.\n- [ ] All three repo configurations (one/two/zero repos) produce the expected repos on inbound\n      tickets and correct routing on outbound ones; checked per configuration.\n- [ ] An outbound update targeting a project outside the configured scope is surfaced in `bridge\n      preview`'s planned mutation set and, on `bridge sync`, raises `CrossProjectTargetError` from the\n      write-path guard and changes nothing; checked by comparing the projects' issue state before and\n      after the refused sync.\n- [ ] A project key never created in the DC instance, when configured in the mapping, makes a bridge\n      pass fail closed and write nothing; checked by asserting the pass errors and a post-run query of\n      the real projects shows no change.\n- [ ] Every scenario's preview contained only targets in its intended project; checked by asserting an\n      empty intersection against every other configured project for each preview.\n- [ ] The whole rehearsal runs green in the `jira-dc-harness` CI job against the ephemeral DC instance;\n      checked by the job passing (not skipped — the fail-on-all-skip canary enforces at least one live\n      scenario executed).\n- [ ] Every scratch project the run created is deleted on teardown and a read of each returns 404,\n      including when a scenario fails mid-run; checked by injecting a post-creation failure into one\n      scenario and asserting all scratch projects are gone (404) after teardown.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/external/live_jira_dc/conftest.py","reason":"add a scratch_projects fixture yielding N verified scratch projects, reusing the in-conftest provisioning in place (nothing relocated, per ccf6 monkeypatch guard)"},{"path":"tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_multi_project_rehearsal.py","reason":"new: the nine DC rehearsal scenarios + per-run fixtures (four scratch projects, isolated DC store copy, DC-pointed bridge config)"},{"path":"docs/jira-sync-setup.md","reason":"runbook: rehearsal now runs against the ephemeral DC instance in CI and locally via make jira-dc-up, replacing the live-Cloud section"},{"path":"tests/external/live_multi_project/conftest.py","reason":"delete: flawed live-Cloud-only draft superseded by the DC rehearsal"},{"path":"tests/external/live_multi_project/test_multi_project_rehearsal.py","reason":"delete: flawed live-Cloud-only draft superseded by the DC rehearsal"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","1734-7c6d-5a6a-48fd"],["depends_on","273a-ae7d-23ac-40c2"],["depends_on","462d-8d84-122a-4812"],["depends_on","4631-5598-7127-4a56"],["depends_on","67f9-4a07-9667-446a"],["depends_on","7032-d9f3-ed89-4f7b"],["depends_on","a33c-9001-9d86-4e59"],["depends_on","c927-0a68-4465-42a2"],["depends_on","ce02-47ed-6505-4925"],["depends_on","cef7-7ac5-18e6-41a3"],["depends_on","d19d-7f60-0137-475a"],["parent","0e68-41eb-5782-4336"],["relates_to","8c08-305f-3faf-489d"],["relates_to","9c22-f26d-47e9-4288"],["relates_to","b4f6-6c5f-1671-4554"],["relates_to","e917-ab1e-a5c3-4994"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"0e68-41eb-5782-4336","parent_status_uuid":"55f65ab7-4c19-4428-84b7-a4494eea1d03","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"368f-f03e-a045-4377","ticket_type":"story","title":"Live multi-project rehearsal against throwaway projects on the ephemeral Jira DC instance","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["87730fc0-b372-4fa6-a705-2f5faa6a2867","ccdd655a-2049-4fb7-9424-1cf0b85ec51c","cfef0d67-a75e-49ba-a1bb-20cd09de3c53","55f65ab7-4c19-4428-84b7-a4494eea1d03","4237eef1-bb63-49d4-bb3a-2bcf2395791f","f3a9f86e-48fa-461a-b3a1-40b6d1214eb4","1bc8e630-2f18-4bb4-ac03-9fb9eb388c35","5e9d8e2c-42b6-453e-9165-cf2a10800a82","14d7c119-6739-45be-b0f6-940609fd3ea4","3060badd-d1b3-4942-b806-09ac4368f32c","9ea8ec2a-62ac-44e1-9c6b-b6be530c8cc9","9d335fb9-592c-4dbe-bf87-2909ec9a32da","4561b6cd-d5c9-4b81-859b-e57b21b63d76","cc415500-bda3-41b9-b845-07456425f071","45b0f7f3-0a64-4d3b-bc89-ea24c6a4e4ed","cac19e6b-3355-4117-b814-44c0bbc344a8","da74379b-c12a-4b01-bd3d-e8d775ce65aa"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786748035798407677,"uuid":"8ff2efd8-8388-4262-ae15-4b506cac032e"}